ing.  \n* The **potentiometer** lets the user set a reference value (e.g., a desired temperature or a brightness level).  \n* The **LCD** (usually a 16\u00d72 character display) shows the current temperature, the set point, and any status messages.  \n\nBelow you\u2019ll find two complete examples:\n\n| Example | Temperature sensor | Potentiometer use | Key features |\n|---------|--------------------|-------------------|--------------|\n| **A** | LM35 (analog) | Sets a *desired temperature* (set\u2011point) | Simple analog read, mapping, and threshold comparison |\n| **B** | DS18B20 (digital 1", "", "### Quick answer\n\n```js\nconst arr", "", ""], "errors": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "max_output_tokens_per_s": 112.0, "max_concurrent_requests": 8, "rtfx": 0.0, "spec_decode_acceptance_rate": 29.11036789297659, "spec_decode_acceptance_length": 2.4555183946488297, "spec_decode_num_drafts": 1495, "spec_decode_draft_tokens": 7475, "spec_decode_accepted_tokens": 2176, "spec_decode_per_position_acceptance_rates": [0.6729096989966555, 0.3759197324414716, 0.2140468227424749, 0.12508361204013377, 0.06755852842809365], "mean_ttft_ms": 169.30994056747295, "median_ttft_ms": 179.1231370298192, "std_ttft_ms": 56.923135673200875, "p50_ttft_ms": 179.1231370298192, "p90_ttft_ms": 212.94265700271353, "p99_ttft_ms": 292.37041564774694, "mean_tpot_ms": 15.67464102588494, "median_tpot_ms": 15.595848405652475, "std_tpot_ms": 2.6296287584390874, "p50_tpot_ms": 15.595848405652475, "p90_tpot_ms": 17.5408099458632, "p99_tpot_ms": 22.488393009335923, "mean_itl_ms": 38.150916743188795, "median_itl_ms": 36.64439800195396, "std_itl_ms": 13.043069429904016, "p50_itl_ms": 36.64439800195396, "p90_itl_ms": 39.3075738567859, "p99_itl_ms": 123.07399016804993, "mean_e2el_ms": 3734.036223759176, "median_e2el_ms": 2694.74099308718, "std_e2el_ms": 3633.8928961997867, "p50_e2el_ms": 2694.74099308718, "p90_e2el_ms": 8584.6403070027, "p99_e2el_ms": 12708.16934509785}